.TH SUD0 1 "October 2026" "sud0 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sud0 \- run a command as root after polkit authorization
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sud0
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ COMMAND " [ARG ...]" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sud0
sends a bounded command request to a root system-bus broker.
The broker derives the caller identity from D-Bus credentials, asks polkit to authorize
.BR nz.passcod.sud0.run ,
and starts a separate systemd transient service running a fixed executor.
No sud0 binary is setuid or setgid.
.PP
Options must appear before
.IR COMMAND .
After the command begins, every remaining word is an argument even when it resembles an option.
Use
.B --
before a command name that begins with a hyphen.
With no command,
.B /bin/bash
is executed directly; command strings are not interpreted by a shell.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-description " " TEXT
Add a human-readable reason to the authentication prompt.
It affects presentation only, not policy or execution.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-chdir " " PATH
Open
.I PATH
before authorization and use that directory object for execution.
Without this option, the invoking current directory is opened and preserved by descriptor.
.TP
.BR \-\-setenv " " NAME[=VALUE]
Set an explicit environment value, or import
.I NAME
from the client environment when no equals sign is present.
May be repeated.
Missing imports, duplicate names, invalid names, and protected names are errors.
.TP
.B \-\-pty
Allocate a pseudo-terminal.
Conflicts with
.BR \-\-pipe .
.TP
.B \-\-pipe
Connect stdin, stdout, and stderr directly without a pseudo-terminal.
Conflicts with
.BR \-\-pty .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-non-interactive
Do not permit polkit to start an interactive authentication challenge.
.B \-\-no-ask-password
is a visible alias.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-validate
Validate or refresh authorization without running a command.
This option conflicts with command, description, directory, environment, and I/O options.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
The action authorizes arbitrary root command execution.
Its default for an active subject is
.BR auth_admin_keep ;
polkit normally retains that authorization for about five minutes.
The retained grant is scoped to the action and equivalent subject rather than command details, so commands can differ during the retained window.
Inactive and other-session subjects use
.BR auth_admin .
.B sud0
does not implement another authorization cache or configurable timeout.
.PP
When interaction is allowed, the client registers
.B /usr/bin/pkttyagent --fallback
for its invoking parent process.
Authentication finishes before PTY mode changes the local terminal to raw mode.
.PP
The packaged prompt has this form:
.PP
.nf
Authentication is required to run as root:
TEXT
ESCAPED-ARGV
in PATH
.fi
.PP
The TEXT line is omitted without a description.
The broker derives PATH from the received directory descriptor, adds an environment-override count when applicable, and adds the request digest when a displayed command or path is truncated.
The authentication agent may add its own surrounding text.
.PP
The root-owned
.B /etc/sud0/prompt.template
controls presentation.
Supported placeholders are
.BR {description} ,
.BR {description_line} ,
.BR {command} ,
.BR {cwd} ,
.BR {cwd_identity} ,
.BR {environment} ,
.BR {environment_line} ,
.BR {request_digest} ,
and
.BR {digest_line} .
An invalid or missing template prevents broker startup.
.SH WORKING DIRECTORY
The opened directory descriptor, not displayed pathname text, determines the execution directory.
This preserves the directory object across a concurrent rename or pathname replacement.
A relative
.B \-D
path is opened relative to the client's current directory.
.SH INPUT AND OUTPUT
When stdin, stdout, and stderr are all terminals, the default is PTY mode; otherwise the default is pipe mode.
Explicit mode options override this choice.
.PP
PTY mode forwards terminal bytes, propagates window dimensions, handles suspend and continue, and restores terminal attributes on exit.
Pipe mode preserves binary streams without allocating a PTY.
.B sud0
emits no terminal tint, title, prompt prefix, or command-output log.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The executor supplies exactly these baseline values before adding accepted explicit variables:
.PP
.nf
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin
HOME=/root
USER=root
LOGNAME=root
SHELL=/bin/bash
.fi
.PP
Baseline and systemd activation names cannot be replaced.
Security-sensitive loader, allocator, language-runtime, and build-tool control-variable families are also rejected.
See
.B SECURITY.md
in the installed documentation for the complete policy.
.PP
A program name containing a slash is executed as given.
A bare program name is searched in the fixed
.B PATH
above.
There is no variable expansion, globbing, or shell parsing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
For a normally exiting command,
.B sud0
returns that command's status from 0 through 255.
For a command terminated by signal
.IR N ,
it returns 128+
.IR N .
When the client catches SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGHUP, or SIGQUIT, it requests cancellation and returns 128 plus the caught signal number after cleanup.
.PP
.B \-\-validate
returns 0 when authorized and 1 when not authorized.
Command denial, cancellation, malformed requests, broker failures, and local setup errors produce a diagnostic on standard error and status 1.
Command-line syntax errors are reported by the option parser with status 2.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/bin/sud0
Unprivileged client.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/sud0/sud0-broker
Root system-bus broker.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/sud0/sud0-exec
Fixed root executor used by transient services.
.TP
.B /etc/sud0/prompt.template
Root-owned authentication prompt template.
.TP
.B /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/nz.passcod.sud0.policy
Polkit action definition.
.TP
.B /usr/share/dbus-1/system.d/nz.passcod.sud0.conf
System-bus ownership and send policy.
.TP
.B /usr/share/dbus-1/system-services/nz.passcod.sud0.service
D-Bus activation entry.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/systemd/system/sud0-broker.service
D-Bus service unit; it is activated on demand and has no install section.
.SH SECURITY
The default prompt discloses arguments, cwd, and descriptions to the authentication agent; a custom template can also disclose environment values and other context.
Rendered details may be recorded by verbose local polkit logging.
Avoid putting secrets there.
Normal broker diagnostics and unit names do not include them.
.PP
Every directory and executable on the fixed root search path must be protected from unprivileged modification.
The broker service is hardened independently; authorized target commands run in separate transient services and do not inherit broker hardening.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
The current implementation requires Linux 5.9 or newer and systemd 257 or newer and targets conventional Arch Linux
.B /usr
paths.
The private D-Bus interface and frozen request format may change during the 0.x series.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Broker activation failures can be inspected with
.B systemctl status sud0-broker.service
and
.BR journalctl -u sud0-broker.service .
A missing bare command should be retried with an absolute pathname or installed on the fixed root search path.
A non-interactive denial requires a retained authorization or a retry without
.BR \-n .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR pkttyagent (1),
.BR polkit (8),
.BR systemd.service (5)
